Volkswagen announced Thursday that it will cut another 50,000 jobs worldwide under its biggest restructuring in the company's 89-year history, as the German carmaker faces pressure from US tariffs, overcapacity and fierce competition from Chinese rivals. The plan also sets out the future of four German plants.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea41b3de-a7d8-11f1-b246-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ed6d620049d2ef529bb6edac6f77fc127b56c26e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea41b3de-a7d8-11f1-b246-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ed6d620049d2ef529bb6edac6f77fc127b56c26e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5407d860-a7f8-11f1-8ec6-8f635c8620e6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 00:34:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ea41b3de-a7d8-11f1-b246-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/ed6d620049d2ef529bb6edac6f77fc127b56c26e.jpg">© Ronny Hartmann, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Tunisia court upholds prison sentences of up to 45 years for opposition figures</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260903-tunisia-court-upholds-prison-sentences-of-up-to-45-years-for-opposition-figures</link><description>
Tunisia's top court on Thursday upheld prison sentences of up to 45 years for opposition leaders, lawyers and businessmen convicted in a major conspiracy case, in a ruling opponents said further entrenches President Kais Saied's authoritarian rule.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be337c3e-a7cc-11f1-9608-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-20T193545Z-1050784693-RC2J2NAHJMOM-RTRMADP-3-TUNISIA-POLITICS-PROTESTS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be337c3e-a7cc-11f1-9608-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-20T193545Z-1050784693-RC2J2NAHJMOM-RTRMADP-3-TUNISIA-POLITICS-PROTESTS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3f00dc22-a7e5-11f1-9b90-75c45f500283</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 22:17:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be337c3e-a7cc-11f1-9608-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-20T193545Z-1050784693-RC2J2NAHJMOM-RTRMADP-3-TUNISIA-POLITICS-PROTESTS.jpg">© Jihed Abidellaoui, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Technology</category><title>Nvidia to buy Hugging Face for $12.93 billion in major AI expansion</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260903-nvidia-to-buy-hugging-face-for-12-93-billion-in-major-ai-expansion</link><description>
Nvidia said Thursday it will buy AI developer platform Hugging Face for $12.93 billion, its latest major investment to expand its influence in open-source artificial intelligence. The deal would bring Nvidia closer to developers and broaden its customer base as tech giants develop chips to reduce reliance on the company.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8e495a4-a7a3-11f1-bd27-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C76F294.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8e495a4-a7a3-11f1-bd27-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C76F294.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3d417e42-a7df-11f1-a641-75c45f500283</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 21:34:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e8e495a4-a7a3-11f1-bd27-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C76F294.jpg">© Matt Ramey, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>'50% savvy political tactics, 50% extraordinarily good luck' - the formula to Meloni's success?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260903-50-savvy-political-tactics-50-extraordinarily-good-luck-the-formula-to-meloni-s-success</link><description>
Giorgia Meloni's hard-right government on Friday becomes the longest-lasting in Italy's postwar history -- a notable record that belies considerable challenges ahead of elections next year. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Nathalie Tocci, Director of the Istituto Affari Internazionali in Rome and Professor of Practice at the John Hopkins University SAIS. She says that Meloni's success comes down to "50 percent savvy political tactics and 50 percent extraordinarily good luck".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0739d9e-a7d8-11f1-9f25-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260903-223116-224348-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0739d9e-a7d8-11f1-9f25-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260903-223116-224348-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0b2740cc-a7da-11f1-9679-db985a0f8f77</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 20:57:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category>Eye on Africa</category><title>Shady surgeons and Nigeria organ harvesting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/shady-surgeons-and-nigeria-organ-harvesting</link><description>
In tonight's edition, legal loopholes and gaps about specialised medicine may be driving Illegal organ harvesting in Nigeria. Also, South Sudan may be moving closer to delivering on elections scheduled for December. And on the islands of São Tomé and Príncipe, six colonial era plantation estates have just been added to the UNESCO World Heritage List.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ab71e1c-a7d3-11f1-a563-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260903-2142-Live-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ab71e1c-a7d3-11f1-a563-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ANGL260903-2142-Live-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f0fc8028-a7d3-11f1-9387-fdf41a79cd1b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 20:15:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Georja CALVIN-SMITH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>El Niño weather phenomenon set to deliver massive blow to global economy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260903-el-ni%C3%B1o-weather-phenomenon-set-to-deliver-massive-blow-to-global-economy</link><description>
The UN warns El Niño is a "supersized" phenomenon that will hit the global economy. UK cider producers are feeling the impact of  drought. Plus, Nvidia buys Hugging Face for $12.9 billion. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/186ddb60-a7d0-11f1-a1ce-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3780429966a99ce7a93b962-65640668.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/186ddb60-a7d0-11f1-a1ce-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3780429966a99ce7a93b962-65640668.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1eeed936-a7cf-11f1-8c2a-c9b691556019</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 19:52:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Camille KNIGHT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>No, UN chief Guterres did not call Francesca Albanese 'out of control'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260903-no-un-chief-guterres-did-not-call-francesca-albanese-out-of-control</link><description>
Pro-Israel lobby group UN Watch alleged that Secretary-General Antonio Guterres referred Francesca Albanese, the UN’s Special Rapporteur on Palestine, "out of control", saying he'd previously called her a "horrible woman." But Guterres named no one in his remarks. He said “many” independent rapporteurs were “totally out of control,” without singling out any individual. The UN has since said linking the comment specifically to Albanese is a “misreading” of his remarks. Vedika Bahl fact-checks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faa1685e-a7ca-11f1-a357-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-447843536a99c5e4f335f7-83392847.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/faa1685e-a7ca-11f1-a357-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-447843536a99c5e4f335f7-83392847.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e3d9dddc-a7c9-11f1-91c8-c9b691556019</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 19:34:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Deadlocked jury in Lindsay Clancy's children murder trial deliberates for sixth day</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/deadlocked-jury-in-lindsay-clancy-s-children-murder-trial-deliberates-for-sixth-day</link><description>
Jurors in the Lindsay Clancy murder trial are deliberating for a sixth day in Plymouth, Massachusetts after twice saying they can’t agree whether the former labor and delivery nurse is criminally responsible for killing her three young children. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6bb47c60-a65a-11f1-abf4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239643451849.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6bb47c60-a65a-11f1-abf4-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26239643451849.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2f74a794-a7c6-11f1-ad3b-65a65d448fea</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 18:44:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>‘Fight through darkness, water’: Nepal survivor recounts escape from flood-hit tunnel</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260903-fight-through-darkness-water-nepal-survivor-recounts-escape-from-flood-hit-tunnel</link><description>
A Nepalese worker recounts his harrowing escape from a hydropower project tunnel after last week's devastating flood. Around 900 workers remain trapped in tunnels at six hydroelectric plants in Nepal as the number of missing in the Himalayan disaster rose to 5,624 on Thursday, according to Nepalese and Chinese authorities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c0b6cb6-a7b0-11f1-962a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T141836Z-1431816270-RC2FBNAICU0M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-TUNNEL-SURVIVOR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c0b6cb6-a7b0-11f1-962a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T141836Z-1431816270-RC2FBNAICU0M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-TUNNEL-SURVIVOR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">38461b4c-a7b1-11f1-952d-dd80a2f2ae2e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 17:22:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7c0b6cb6-a7b0-11f1-962a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-03T141836Z-1431816270-RC2FBNAICU0M-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS-TUNNEL-SURVIVOR.jpg">© Joseph Campbell, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Anti-Christian murder in Syria? No indication he was killed because of his faith</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-anti-christian-murder-syria-no-indication-killed-faith</link><description>
A Christian man by the name of Nader Boulos Tannous was murdered in Homs, Syria on August 15, 2026. After his death, Israel, Greece and Cyprus were quick to denounce what they called an anti-Christian act. Several days later however, authorities in Homs said the suspect had admitted killing Tannous as part of a personal dispute going back to 2012.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efbc11e2-a2f6-11f1-bfe9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-11-2.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efbc11e2-a2f6-11f1-bfe9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-11-2.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">03e99b86-a6a7-11f1-a89b-73cec2680c44</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 17:00:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/efbc11e2-a2f6-11f1-bfe9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Mod%C3%A8le-1920-x-1080-11-2.png">© Montage by the Observers </source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>WMO chief says El Nino could be strongest in four decades</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-wmo-chief-says-el-nino-could-be-strongest-in-four-decades</link><description>
El Nino could be the strongest since records began four decades ago, the United Nations' climate agency warned Thursday, with the UN chief warning the world is in the "danger zone of extreme weather". The naturally-occurring weather phenomenon is set to become "very strong" in the months ahead and is near certain to persist through to February, the World Meteorological Organization (WMO) said. FRANCE 24's Journalist Carys Garland tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/38b9cb56-a7b0-11f1-a853-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260903-160049-160552-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/38b9cb56-a7b0-11f1-a853-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260903-160049-160552-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3d82e4d8-a7b0-11f1-8996-3557bba3da42</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 16:11:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Two Palestinian teens killed in West Bank raid by Israeli settlers and army</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-two-palestinian-teens-killed-in-west-bank-raid-by-israeli-settlers-and-army</link><description>
Two Palestinian teenagers ⁠were killed on ​Wednesday in an attack by Israeli settler militants and ​army troops on their village in the occupied West Bank, local officials and the Palestinian health ministry said, amid an uptick in violence ​by ‌Jewish settlers in the territory. The Israeli military said in a statement its forces had entered al-Mughayyir to ​provide security for police officers and an Israeli ‌civilian seeking to retrieve livestock.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b373ca80-a7b1-11f1-96ad-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5511377526a999b7c3d5ae9-14846200.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b373ca80-a7b1-11f1-96ad-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5511377526a999b7c3d5ae9-14846200.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5dfc7742-a7b0-11f1-a9f5-3557bba3da42</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 16:09:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US energy firms dominate Venezuela deals worth billions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-us-energy-firms-dominate-venezuela-deals-worth-billions</link><description>
US energy firms on Wednesday signed a raft of multi-billion-dollar deals with Venezuela, days after the South American country agreed to grant the United States control of a huge chunk of its vast oil reserves. President Donald Trump has talked up the agreement on Venezuela's oil reserves as the "biggest oil deal in world history." But the deals have raised major questions about Venezuela's sovereignty, as FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/caef27aa-a7b0-11f1-97f4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260903-161524-162126-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/caef27aa-a7b0-11f1-97f4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260903-161524-162126-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d2d70672-a7b0-11f1-9ec9-3557bba3da42</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 16:06:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France agriculture production sees economic hit from heatwaves</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-france-agriculture-production-sees-economic-hit-from-heatwaves</link><description>
France's recent heatwaves didn't just pose enormous health risks, they also hampered the economy. Authorities have estimated that the recent heat and drought caused production to plummet and expect wealth generated by the agricultural sector to decline by 8% over the course of the year. The knock-on effects will cost the French economy an estimated 0.1 percentage points of growth in 2026.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28f689d4-a7b0-11f1-a46a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260903-160820-160955-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28f689d4-a7b0-11f1-a46a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260903-160820-160955-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2dda3d88-a7b0-11f1-bd79-3557bba3da42</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 16:05:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US feminist icon and journalist Gloria Steinem dies aged 92</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-us-feminist-icon-and-journalist-gloria-steinem-dies-aged-92</link><description>
The co-founder of Ms. Magazine and celebrated feminist icon Gloria Steinem has died at her home at the age of 92. An internationally recognised activist in the fight for women's equality, she spoke out for the legalisation of abortion, same-sex marriage, and equal pay. She began her journalism career in New York in the 1960s. Politically, she was an outspoken critic of Donald Trump, arguing that the US had taken many steps back when it came to women's rights. FRANCE 24's Journalist and host of "The 51%" tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b6f07a4-a7ac-11f1-ab68-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-19578318936a99929fc2c8d6-44317367.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b6f07a4-a7ac-11f1-ab68-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-19578318936a99929fc2c8d6-44317367.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">273acb18-a7a2-11f1-8808-a1a1fffc616f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 15:39:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Why Ukraine’s drained Kakhovka Dam is strategic for Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-why-ukraine-drained-kakhovka-dam-strategic-russia</link><description>
Small groups of Russian soldiers have been inching forward through the vast, drained Kakhovka reservoir since they blew up the dam in June 2023. Russian forces are infiltrating this “no man’s land” for reconnaissance purposes rather than for a future military offensive, said a military expert.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b33f7b0-a6f0-11f1-bf9f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23190746580401.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b33f7b0-a6f0-11f1-bf9f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23190746580401.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e40a770-a6ef-11f1-bc77-819a99e6cab5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 15:34:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b33f7b0-a6f0-11f1-bf9f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23190746580401.jpg">© Evgeniy Maloletka, AP</source><dc:creator>Sonya CIESNIK</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Giorgia Meloni government becomes Italy's longest-lasting since World War II</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-giorgia-meloni-government-becomes-italy-s-longest-lasting-since-world-war-ii</link><description>
Italy's first female Prime Minister, Giorgia Meloni, has surpassed a longevity record set by the late Silvio Berlusconi. When she took office in 2022, many European allies viewed her with unease, given her party's neo-fascist roots. Yet she has governed pragmatically, working within EU institutions and even supporting Ukraine. Domestically, however, she has targeted same-sex parents and clamped down on press freedom.
